# Optional locally, expected in deployment.
#
# The download button reads the newest release from the public GitHub API, which
# allows 60 unauthenticated requests per hour PER IP. On your own machine that
# budget is yours alone and you will never touch it. On a hosted build — CI
# runners, serverless platforms — the address is shared with everyone else on
# the box, so an unauthenticated lookup is likely to be refused.
#
# That failure is quiet and it lasts: a rate-limited lookup falls back to the
# release pinned in src/lib/release.ts, and `cacheLife('hours')` caches the
# fallback exactly as durably as a success. One 403 therefore serves a stale
# version, size and digest for the whole revalidation window, and the build
# stays green throughout.
#
# Any classic token with no scopes, or a fine-grained token with public read
# access, is enough.
GITHUB_TOKEN=""
